                 - Applied to all ground units, granting a 46.875% chance to evade ranged attacks when attacked from lower elevations.
                 - Missed attacks are visually offset toward the ground in front of the unit, in the direction of the attacker.
                 - Splash damage misses are hardcoded in this system and require specific effect tree changes to work.
                 - The 1/256 equal-elevation miss chance from the original game is not replicated in SC: Evo.
                ---
                Shrub Vision (Concealed)
                 - Can be painted via the Terrain Editor or applied through doodads like Vents or Tall Grass that have Shrub Vision in their footprints.
                 - If both the attacker and defender are within Shrub Vision, attacks can still miss.
                ---
                &quot;Fake High Ground&quot; replicates doodads (e.g., trees) that provided cover in the original game.
                 - Implemented using pre-placed regions to simulate cover.
                 - Unlike Shrub Vision, units can still be targeted without requiring vision of the area.
                 - The &quot;SCEvo: Register Miss Chance Region&quot; trigger action allows regions to be used by this system.
                 - Regions named &quot;HighGround_X&quot; (0-16) are automatically registered.
                 - If both the attacker and defender are within any Fake High Ground region, attacks can still miss.
                ---
                Fake High Ground Shrub
                 -Applied when a location has both Shrub Vision and Terrain Custom Attribute 1.
                 - Simulates higher cliff levels without needing to modify actual cliff height.
                 - Attacks will NOT be evaded if the attacker is also within the Fake High Ground Shrub or is an air unit.
                 - Used to create high-ground features in maps like Polypoid.
                ---
                Note: 
                - Ranged weapons must be edited with the &quot;NeverMiss&quot; option flag set to Disabled
                 -- Expect splash damage weapons like Siege Tank or Archon, which use hardcoded detection for miss chance.
                - For units that transition between air and ground (e.g., Terran structures, Viking), use &quot;SCBW_MissChance@AB&quot; &amp; &quot;SCBW_MissChance@ClearBuffs&quot; --
                  -- Effect entries in the Morph Start/Finish effects to apply or clear miss chance appropriately.
                - Structures cannot gain Shrub Vision miss chance. This prevents issues on maps without proper shrub pathing blockers.
                - Defiler Dark Swarm is independent of this system and does not require Miss Chance to be enabled.
                - Miss Chance visual implementation requires the use of specific &quot;GenericAttackWhiff&quot; &amp; &quot;GenericAttackMissileWhiff&quot; actor actions
                 - Units with multiple visual components tied to a single attack (e.g., Scout) require additional sequencing macros for correct visuals.
                 -- Search for &quot;WhiffSequence&quot; in Scout or in Multi mod Thor or Reaper data for examples.
            </Comment>
