        <Element Type="Category" Id="2F34F9F0">
            <Identifier>ReadMe</Identifier>
            <Label Type="Label" Library="Ntve" Id="1D55A90E"/>
            <Item Type="Comment" Library="SCEV" Id="BFFF8B27"/>
        </Element>
        <Element Type="Comment" Id="BFFF8B27">
            <Comment>
                Only works in Legacy Mode
                Legacy Selection limits the Unit selection to 12 and 1 Structure at a time, also hides Control Group buttons, Idle Worker and All army buttons are disabled aswell.
                Full implementation requires &apos;IndividualSubgroups&apos; flag to be enable for structures, without this there can be a frame in-between selection updates where you can control multiple structures, --
                -this can&apos;t be changed on run time so it&apos;s disabled in Legacy mod currently.
                Structure implementation only works in Singleplayer, as they are marked as Unselectable until they are highlighted with mouse or when a drag selection is detected.
                Unit are also marked as Highlightable so unit selection can add select the highlighted unit via Ctrl click action
                Both structures and normal units requires &apos;NoHighlightEvent&apos; flag to be turned OFF  in unit flags for this system to function. (Set in Legacy not in Core)
                Drag Selection detection also only works with default hotkeys (left click)
                Control groups are also tracked and limited.
                Selection groups are not sorted in the same way they are in SC1, same 12 units will always be selected regardless of their current world position.
                12 Unit selection can be made to support multiplayer, but currently only setup for Player 1 as the User.
            </Comment>
        </Element>
